# Alt 1 — Unified identity menu

**One row. Click opens a single popover that holds org switching *and* account actions.** (Linear / Vercel pattern.)

The bottom shrinks from two stacked cards to **one** identity row: user avatar + name, org as the secondary line. Everything else lives behind one click.

### Resting

```
│  …nav…                        │
├───────────────────────────────┤
│ ╭───────────────────────────╮ │
│ │ (GD) Greg Daniels      ⌄ │ │
│ │      Acme Inc             │ │
│ ╰───────────────────────────╯ │
└───────────────────────────────┘
```

### Clicked (popover opens upward)

```
   ╭─────────────────────────────╮
   │ ORGANIZATION                │
   │  ✓ Acme Inc                 │
   │    Globex Corp              │
   │  + New organization         │
   ├─────────────────────────────┤
   │ greg@acme.com               │
   │  ⚙  Settings                │
   │  ↗  Sign out                │
   ╰─────────────────────────────╯
┌───────────────────────────────┐
│ (GD) Greg Daniels         ⌃  │
│      Acme Inc                 │
└───────────────────────────────┘
```

### Collapsed sidebar
Just the avatar; same popover on click.

```
│ (GD) │
```

**Pros:** one resting affordance, both concerns in one place, scales to more account actions.
**Cons:** org switch is now two clicks deep; the org name competes with the user name for the second line's meaning.
